# Cheaper and better in Russian: дешевле, гораздо лучше
subtitle: "Compare in Russian: деше́вле, доро́же, важне́е; чем or the of-form; гора́здо лу́чше, всё доро́же and как мо́жно скоре́е."
tags: ["russian","russian comparatives","дешевле","гораздо","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/comparatives"]
thumb: "band \"Cheaper or better?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"A fourteenth Russian story: the wedding banquet","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/140-russian-review-14.cast"}

## Cheaper and better in Russian: дешевле, гораздо лучше
